/description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sir-deadlines-extended-in-5-states-delhi-ec-sets-new-dates-for-final-rolls/articleshow/135326406.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sir-deadlines-extended-in-5-states-delhi-ec-sets-new-dates-for-final-rolls/articleshow/135326406.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-29T23:41:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135326594,imgsize-98916.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jamia sets date for student union poll, revokes disciplinary action against protesters]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jamia-sets-date-for-student-union-poll-revokes-disciplinary-action-against-protesters/articleshow/135324813.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135324813.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jamia-sets-date-for-student-union-poll-revokes-disciplinary-action-against-protesters/articleshow/135324813.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jamia-sets-date-for-student-union-poll-revokes-disciplinary-action-against-protesters/articleshow/135324813.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-29T22:39:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vivek Dubey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135325112,imgsize-321402.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Transgressions by China happen, it's not new': Arunachal CM says no intrusion along LAC]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/transgressions-by-china-happen-its-not-new-arunachal-cm-says-no-intrusion-along-lac/articleshow/135324392.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135324392.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Pema Khandu asserted that border transgressions along the India-China frontier have been a longstanding issue, highlighting China's non-recognition of the McMahon Line. He described the recent confrontations as transgressions instead of intrusions and reassured citizens of the state's stability. Likewise, Union tourism minister Gajendra Singh Shekhawat reaffirmed the safety of India's borders while working to alleviate media-induced tensions regarding the situation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/transgressions-by-china-happen-its-not-new-arunachal-cm-says-no-intrusion-along-lac/articleshow/135324392.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/transgressions-by-china-happen-its-not-new-arunachal-cm-says-no-intrusion-along-lac/articleshow/135324392.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-29T22:37:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pallavi</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135324916,imgsize-72534.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Keeping a list of names': Abhishek Banerjee warns cops trying to 'please' Suvendu]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/keeping-a-list-of-names-abhishek-banerjee-warns-cops-trying-to-please-suvendu/articleshow/135324197.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135324197.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/keeping-a-list-of-names-abhishek-banerjee-warns-cops-trying-to-please-suvendu/articleshow/135324197.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/keeping-a-list-of-names-abhishek-banerjee-warns-cops-trying-to-please-suvendu/articleshow/135324197.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-29T22:15:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vivek Dubey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135324313,imgsize-88392.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Don't push us': SC warns of harsh stand on firecrackers if orders go unenforced]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-push-us-sc-warns-of-harsh-stand-on-firecrackers-if-orders-go-unenforced/articleshow/135321333.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135321333.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Supreme Court tackled the persistent air pollution crisis in Delhi-NCR, stressing the importance of adhering to current firecracker laws. Authorities were cautioned against inaction, as deteriorating air quality poses a threat to public health. The bench underlined the necessity for collaboration among all parties to effectively manage firecracker usage. Measures taken by the Delhi government include restrictions on older vehicles and staggered work hours.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-push-us-sc-warns-of-harsh-stand-on-firecrackers-if-orders-go-unenforced/articleshow/135321333.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-push-us-sc-warns-of-harsh-stand-on-firecrackers-if-orders-go-unenforced/articleshow/135321333.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-29T20:39:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135321386,imgsize-80330.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Educated voters don't turn up in assembly polls': UP minister OP Rajbhar plays down MLC results]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/educated-voters-dont-turn-up-in-assembly-po